WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.080
Is it true that you,

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.850
one of your toughest phone calls

3
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.460
was of all that you had to deal with,

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.440
was about your pregnancy?

5
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.460
I was, I wanna say eight weeks pregnant,

6
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.460
the story I tell about being in Buckingham Palace,

7
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.293
three days later,

8
00:00:16.293 --> 00:00:17.970
the story breaks about Anthony

9
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.780
being in communication online with other women.

10
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.410
And two days later,

11
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.900
I get a phone call from my friend, Felipe.

12
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.919
He said, this is a very awkward conversation for me,

13
00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:28.620
but The New York Times has called

14
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.880
and they're about to report that you're pregnant.

15
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.910
And is there anything you want to share?

16
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:34.743
And he obviously didn't know.

17
00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:37.560
And I was so mad, I had so much rage,

18
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.004
I felt like this deep, this secret, I hadn't told anybody.

19
00:00:41.004 --> 00:00:43.970
We told our parents and our siblings.

20
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:48.110
And so he said, do you want to tell Hillary,

21
00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:48.943
do you want to call people?

22
00:00:48.943 --> 00:00:51.590
I said, no, I dare them, I dare them to run this story.

23
00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.170
I'm not even 12 weeks pregnant.

24
00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:56.630
And of course they did, and I was so shattered,

25
00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.960
I was so broken by not being able to share,

26
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.550
what for me was a once in a lifetime gift.

27
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.383
Yes.

28
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:05.240
That till today, today,

29
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.270
and I did it yesterday in the kitchen,

30
00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.500
that I wander around,

31
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.080
and when I'm in the shower or shopping,

32
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.450
I'll just say I'm pregnant.

33
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:15.277
And I say it because I never got to say it before.

34
00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.700
And yesterday, Jordan said to me, mommy, you're pregnant?

35
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.620
And I'm like, no, no, no, no.

36
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.280
But it reminds you that there are things

37
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.850
that do stay with you.

38
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.170
I so appreciate hearing that

39
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.170
because it's not always what you expect is the moment.

40
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.370
Here's what I mean.

41
00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.030
So when I got that phone call from Chris Miller

42
00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:43.993
of I got to tell you something, something is coming out,

43
00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.440
it wasn't the pregnancy, I feared,

44
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.950
it was being caught drinking.

45
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.433
And I felt like this was my shame.

46
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.793
And I was almost relieved when it wasn't that.

47
00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:04.810
When people find out your deepest, darkest secrets,

48
00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.640
and I experienced that when I was 13 years old,

49
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.230
and got outed and thrown into an institution

50
00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:16.230
and career over, I have such PTSD from that,

51
00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.270
that I think if someone's gonna catch me drinking again,

52
00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.060
I'm going to lose my career,

53
00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.060
I'm gonna lose my job that I love so much.

54
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.470
And it's so traumatizing.

55
00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:32.470
And that was my thing, and it carries with it so much shame.

56
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.600
How did you deal with that?

57
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.960
The first time Anthony and I sat down after his first,

58
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.212
you know, the first revelation about his communication

59
00:02:41.212 --> 00:02:42.663
with women online,

60
00:02:44.202 --> 00:02:46.110
and we went away, we went to Texas, to therapy.

61
00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.210
I didn't understand anything,

62
00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.170
I didn't understand anything about, you know,

63
00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.810
behavior that you couldn't control,

64
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.000
I didn't understand addiction,

65
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.940
I didn't know anybody growing up, really,

66
00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.310
who were divorced or split up,

67
00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.000
these weren't things you talked about in the Middle East.

68
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.200
I felt like the minute it was all out,

69
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.020
he seemed so relieved.

70
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.690 line:15%
It was almost like an unburdening.

71
00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.270 line:15%
And he said, well, how do I stop the behavior?

72
00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.103 line:15%
And how do I fix it?

73
00:03:09.103 --> 00:03:10.950 line:15%
And I fully believed he could knock it off,

74
00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.620
100% thought, in 2011, when this first happened,

75
00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.570
he could just stop.

76
00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.760
And then we learned later

77
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.680
when he ran for mayor of New York City in 2013,

78
00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.960
when there was another revelation,

79
00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.080
that he clearly couldn't stop it.

80
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.610
So every time I would get a call,

81
00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.530
whether it was from Anthony or Felipe, as we talked about,

82
00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.400
every time it was a call or a text saying

83
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.030
this tabloid called, or I have to tell you something,

84
00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.380
it is, well, how bad is it?

85
00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.070
And living in this world of,

86
00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.940
it's not going to be as bad as I think it is,

87
00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:39.260
it's going to be worse, because it always was.

88
00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.820
And that's why in 2019,

89
00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.950
and I do share the story in the book of really

90
00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.330
when I got to the end of my, I couldn't, you know,

91
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.540
I contemplated stepping off a subway platform.

92
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.400
It was really my low of the low.

93
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.760
And when I did that,

94
00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.440
there were two things that really came to me,

95
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.820
was number one, all of this holding everything,

96
00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:01.130
and all of this anger and bitterness was only hurting me.

97
00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.160
Something I later learned with Anthony in therapy

98
00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.840
is that while pain might be necessary,

99
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.860
suffering is optional.

100
00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.420
We have to go to another commercial really quickly,

101
00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.192
but we will be right back.

